Build a products admin on top of an existing REST API at /api/products (fields: id number, name text up to 80 characters, sku text, price number ≥ 0, status active or archived). Declare the typed endpoints with api(). A products page lists the products with a search box and a status filter, says when nothing matches, and has a form to create a product. Each product links to its detail page at /products/<id>, which shows the product, lets the user edit it with the same validated form and delete it. Cover loading, error and empty states.

Start from the crud recipe in bench/recipes/crud (CRUD from an api() schema). It already passes brain check, brain doctor and brain test in a fresh brain_new app. Its files are below, each with its path relative to the app root: after brain_new, write them as they are (they replace the scaffold files with the same path), then adapt names, routes and texts to the brief, keeping the structure and the tests passing.
Recipe notes: api() is the typed client of an existing backend at /api/items; responses are validated against Item. Link /items from the nav.

