Build a sales dashboard at /dashboard. A period switch (last 7, 30 and 90 days) changes everything on the page. Four KPI cards show revenue, orders, new customers and refund rate, each with its change against the previous period (up in green, down in red, the direction readable by screen readers). Below, a table of sales per product (product, orders, revenue) can be sorted by clicking each column header. Take the numbers from a deterministic demo data module in lib/.

Start from the dashboard recipe in bench/recipes/dashboard (Dashboard: KPIs + sortable table). It already passes brain check, brain doctor and brain test in a fresh brain_new app. Its files are below, each with its path relative to the app root: after brain_new, write them as they are (they replace the scaffold files with the same path), then adapt names, routes and texts to the brief, keeping the structure and the tests passing.
Recipe notes: Uses its own comp/data-table instead of the kit <Table>, which currently fails `brain build` (B0116). Link /dashboard from the nav.

=== lib/dashboard-data.jsbrain ===
// Demo numbers for the dashboard, deterministic per period. Replace with a resource() over an api() endpoint.
export default function dashboardData(period) {
  const f = period === '90d' ? 12 : period === '30d' ? 4 : 1
  return {
    kpis: [
      { id: 'revenue', label: 'Revenue', value: 12400 * f, unit: '$', delta: 8.2 },
      { id: 'orders', label: 'Orders', value: 310 * f, unit: '', delta: 3.1 },
      { id: 'customers', label: 'New customers', value: 42 * f, unit: '', delta: -4.5 },
      { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refund rate', value: 1.8, unit: '%', delta: 0 },
    ],
    rows: [
      { id: 1, product: 'Starter plan', orders: 120 * f, revenue: 2280 * f },
      { id: 2, product: 'Pro plan', orders: 95 * f, revenue: 5605 * f },
      { id: 3, product: 'Team plan', orders: 40 * f, revenue: 3960 * f },
      { id: 4, product: 'Add-on storage', orders: 55 * f, revenue: 555 * f },
    ],
  }
}

=== ui/kpi.brain ===
<meta props="label:str value:num unit:str='' delta:num?">

<script>
  // delta: change vs the previous period in %, positive is good · the direction is spelled out for screen readers
  const shown = drv(() => (unit === '$' ? '$' + value.toLocaleString('en-US') : value.toLocaleString('en-US') + unit))
  const dir = drv(() => (delta == null ? '' : delta > 0 ? 'up' : delta < 0 ? 'down' : 'flat'))
</script>

<article class="kpi">
  <p class="name">{label}</p>
  <p class="value">{shown}</p>
  {#if delta != null}
    <p class="delta" class:up={delta > 0} class:down={delta < 0}>
      <span aria-hidden="true">{delta > 0 ? '▲' : delta < 0 ? '▼' : '•'}</span>
      {Math.abs(delta)}% <span class="sr">{dir}</span> vs previous period
    </p>
  {/if}
</article>

